<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Frederick I, Duke of Württemberg</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1557–1608</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Frederick I of Württemberg-Mömpelgard</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Frederick I, Duke of Württemberg, ruled the County of Montbéliard from 1581 and inherited the Duchy of Württemberg in 1593. A Lutheran prince with wide interests, he employed the architect <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/heinrich-schickhardt">Heinrich Schickhardt</a>, who rebuilt much of Montbéliard and founded the new town of Freudenstadt. He strengthened ducal power against the Württemberg estates.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/frederick-i-duke-of-wurttemberg.jpg" alt="Frederick I, Duke of Württemberg" width="236" height="332" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Friedrich_I,_Herzog_von_W%C3%BCrttemberg_(1557-1608).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
